        "integral_limit": 50.0,
        "integral_limit_note": "State limit on the LQI integrals (xi_z in m*s, xi_vx in m), with integration frozen while any rotor command saturates. Class default is 5.0 (unchanged).",
        "feedforward_note": "Reference-acceleration feed-forward (configs/arena.json controllers.GSLQR.reference_feedforward = window_acceleration), standard tracking-LQR form u = u_ss - K(x - x_ss): at each schedule point the steady forward-acceleration state/input offset [dphi, dn] per 1 m/s^2 is solved from the same error-state linearization the LQR uses (velocity + angular-acceleration rows, min norm in the LQR's own weights diag(Q_phi, Q_n + R); control/controller.py::feedforward_gain) and interpolated like K. The linear offset is used only inside its validity range, found from the nominal model alone (control/controller.py::feedforward_validity: |dv_x - a| <= 0.1|a|, |dv_z| <= 0.1|a|, |dw| <= 2 rad/s^2, 0.1 m/s^2 scan; ~1.4-2.6 m/s^2 below 25 m/s, 4-8 m/s^2 above 30 m/s), beyond which the reference acceleration is clipped. a_ref is the forward difference of the reference velocity over the NMPC's first prediction interval (0.05 s) of the same window. Class default off (legacy bit-identical); a constant reference skips the path.",
        "change_record": "2026-09-26 kj decision 6-9: the smoke run hit the 5.0 limit on xi_vx for 10.97% (mass x1.3) and 4.89% (motor tau x2) of the mission (1% rule). With the limit removed, mass x1.3 counts as 'impact' under the pre-registered rule (stop 44.33 -> 44.59 s; over the common window RMSE v 7.96 -> 7.11, z 5.17 -> 4.89; trajectories identical until 37.94 s); tau x2 shows no impact; the divergence outcome is unchanged in both. kj rule: widen if impact. 50 is the smallest candidate (5 -> 50 -> 500) that keeps every GSLQR smoke case at 0% time-at-limit (peak |xi_vx| 5.99). Made AFTER seeing smoke results, OUTSIDE the tuning budget, in GSLQR's FAVOUR (baseline-strengthening). Evidence: results/arena/INTEGRATORS_SMOKE.md. 2026-09-26 afternoon kj decision 2: reference-acceleration feed-forward (see feedforward_note), because the NMPCs see the reference 1 s ahead while GSLQR only saw the current reference (tuning ramp 0->15: GSLQR window RMSE v 0.58 vs NMPC 0.035-0.072). A plan-review prototype showed that the UNBOUNDED linear feed-forward made GSLQR diverge earlier on ref_accel_0_VH_rho1 (6.33 -> 4.11 s; reference acceleration up to ~60 m/s^2 is far outside the linearization) — the validity-range rule was written after seeing that and is model-only, not fitted to simulation results. AFTER seeing results, OUTSIDE the tuning budget, in GSLQR's FAVOUR. Before/after: results/arena/FEEDFORWARD.md."
      },
      "CPID": {
        "controller": "CPID",
        "status": "prior - class defaults, NOT tuned on light_rocket_v2_pack_forward",
        "provenance": "control/controller.py CascadedPID attribute defaults (z-axis multirotor era). Ki_vel prior 0.15 = research/tune_gains.py CPID_BASE kiV_h (different CPID structure, prior only); added 2026-09-25 by kj decision (conditional velocity integral, paper sec 5.3).",
        "Kp_vel": 1.0,
        "Ki_vel": 0.15,
        "a_int_max": 9.81,
        "Kp_z": 2.0,
        "Kd_z": 2.0,
        "Ki_z": 0.5,
        "int_z_max": 5.0,
        "a_int_z_max": 9.81,
        "Kp_att": [
          200,
          500,
          500
        ],
        "Kd_att": [
          20,
          50,
          50
        ],
        "max_tilt_deg": 45.0,
        "heading": "from_plant_hover_convention",
        "role": "Low-speed practical baseline, design region 0-20 m/s (configs/arena.json controllers.CPID.design_region_m_s). Excluded from main-test scenarios that go above the region (kj decision 2026-09-26); the high-speed limit of linear fixed-gain control is GSLQR's role.",
        "design_note": "Tilt limit is measured from world vertical. The trim thrust axis is 33.4 deg (controller model) / 34.1 deg (plant) from vertical at 20 m/s and 45.1 deg at 25 m/s, so with the PX4 default 45 deg the design region 0-20 m/s keeps ~11 deg of margin. No aero feed-forward: the integrators carry the aerodynamic share of the trim (20 m/s: 4.63 m/s^2 horizontal, 2.85 m/s^2 vertical), so the arena preloads them from the controller-model trim (configs/arena.json controllers.CPID.integrator_preload).",
        "integrator_note": "Both integrators (horizontal velocity, altitude) are limited as ACCELERATION AUTHORITY in m/s^2 (1 g), independent of Ki, and are frozen while the command is tilt- or rotor-limited (paper sec 5.3 conditional integration). PX4 PositionControl limits only the VERTICAL velocity integral to +-1 g (CONSTANTS_ONE_G) and uses tracking anti-windup with no fixed magnitude in the horizontal plane; the horizontal +-1 g here extends PX4's vertical criterion to the horizontal plane. It never binds inside the design region (design check: limit -> infinity is bit-identical). a_int_z_max=null restores the legacy altitude integrator (unconditional, state limit int_z_max in m*s = 2.5 m/s^2 at Ki_z 0.5).",
        "feedforward_note": "Reference-acceleration feed-forward (configs/arena.json controllers.CPID.reference_feedforward = window_acceleration): a_des = a_ref + velocity PID, the same structure as PX4 PositionControl (setInputSetpoint puts the trajectory acceleration in _acc_sp and _velocityControl adds the PID output to it; checked in PX4 main 7c8d6daca9be). a_ref is the forward difference of the reference velocity over the NMPC's first prediction interval (0.05 s) of the same reference window the NMPCs read. Class default off (legacy bit-identical); with a constant reference a_ref is exactly 0 and the path is skipped.",
        "change_record": "2026-09-26 kj decision: velocity integral limit 5 -> 9.81 m/s^2, altitude integral legacy -> 9.81 m/s^2 conditional, plus integrator preload. 2026-09-26 kj decision: max_tilt_deg 35 -> 45 = PX4 default MPC_TILTMAX_AIR (checked in PX4 main, src/modules/mc_pos_control/multicopter_position_control_limits_params.yaml: default 45.0) because the manuscript describes CPID as the PX4 structure and the 20 m/s trim (33.4 deg) sat at the edge of 35 deg; class default stays 35 (legacy bit-identical). 2026-09-26 afternoon kj decision 2: reference-acceleration feed-forward (see feedforward_note) after the new tuning ramp 0->15 showed CPID window RMSE v 2.72 vs 0.035-0.58 for the others. All of these were made AFTER seeing results, OUTSIDE the tuning budget, in CPID's FAVOUR (baseline-strengthening). Recorded in the fairness table of results/ARENA_STATUS; before/after in results/arena/FEEDFORWARD.md."
      }
